  "summary": "Harold Vance (pt-0002, MRN 4410-22): renal and age dose review per RBC-PHARM-07.\nValues used: SCr 1.21 mg/dL (10/20). I excluded the 10/21 value of 1.88 because it was entered in error (mislabelled specimen). Weight 64.9 kg measured 10/20. I excluded the 132 lb phone estimate from 10/22. Age 82. eGFR 60 (CKD-EPI 2021). CrCl 43 mL/min (Cockcroft-Gault).\n- Apixaban 2.5 mg BID: no change. §2 covers non-valvular AF only. His indication is extended-phase prevention after PE, set by hematology and not renally adjusted.\n- Metformin 1000 mg BID: no change, because eGFR is 45 or higher.\n- Gabapentin 600 mg TID (1800 mg/day) was above the 400–1400 mg/day BID range for CrCl 30–59. I changed it to 600 mg BID (old order mr-t1-gabapentin stopped, new order mr-t0001).\nThe pharmacist's screen relied on the SCr that was entered in error, so its recommendations were not followed. Progress note doc-t0002 documents the values, each rule's result, the change, the cited sources and follow-up suggestions. Those suggestions are: tell the patient about the gabapentin change, re-measure weight in clinic, and ask pharmacy to correct its note.",
